name syzygy-lines
match *.rtbw
# A table of the set, decoded (input decode syzygy, src/chess_syzygy.c): the best-play lines the tables give from the
# positions of its material that recorded games and openings reach, read from the database this ingest loads into. A
# line is written as the PGN a game of it is, [FEN "P0"], its moves and its result under the 50-move rule, and read as
# a game is (chess.c, grammar pgn, records played): the line [P0, M0, P1, ..., Pn], and for each move the [P, M, P'] a
# game that plays it claims, scored for the side that moves. So a tablebase line converges with the games that stand on
# it and with the other lines that share its tail, by identity alone. No verdict of a position is written: a verdict is
# a read of the tables (laplace tablebase).
grammar pgn
records played
input decode syzygy
